# Lune Design System 2 (web)

When designing, building, or changing the Touch **web** dashboard, treat
`web/design-system/` (`DESIGN.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `tokens/tokens.json`,
`css/lune-ui.src.css`) as the authority. Build pages via `web/touch-ui/` after
`examples/v6` patterns. Do not cite external platform guidelines.

LVGL (`packages/display/`) gets its theme (`lune_theme.h`, `tokens.generated.yaml`),
`lune_design_tokens.h` and brand marks from sibling `../lune-design-system`
(`display` in `tokens/tokens.json`, `tokens/brand.json`) via `lds.yaml` /
`make design-tokens` (`tools/lds_display.py`). Never hand-edit those files.

## Required (web)

1. Use DS2 tokens and components only — no raw hex/px outside the scales.
2. Shell: mode × scope radios, `section.view#v-{dash|conf}-{house|rN}`, panels.
3. No sidebar, no modals, no JS navigation. Forms use `form.panel` + `data-save`.
4. All strings from `web/touch-ui/i18n/`. Destructive actions behind `details.confirm`.
5. Rebuild with `make touch-ui` (calls `lds_build.py config/touch.json`).

## Do not

- Nested cards, decorative glass/gradient chrome, network font fetches
- Hand-editing `web/design-system/dist/**` or generated firmware embeds
- Reintroducing the old SPA shell (`web/dashboard-src`)
